## Summary of Root Causes & Fixes

| # | Root Cause | Fix Applied | File |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| 1 | **Primary**: Open/streaming code blocks got a new content-based hash every tick → Vue destroyed and recreated `Code`+`CodeViewer` on each streamed line → `showCode` reset to `undefined`/`false` on every remount → Collapsible collapsed, hiding updates | Streaming blocks now use a **structural hash** (`type:fileName:index`) that stays stable across streaming ticks | `markdownParser.js` |
| 2 | **Secondary**: `showCode` defaulted to `this.$props.showCodeOpened` (undefined) instead of `true` — so every fresh mount (from key change) collapsed the viewer | Default `showCode = true` when `showCodeOpened` is not explicitly set | `CodeViewer.vue` |

